{
  "supported": true,
  "coverage": "partial",
  "coverage_explanation": "Tests independently establish the lower bound without assuming an initial count, then verify individual increments, decrements, both bounds, blocked overflow, and recovery after boundary attempts. Alarm frequency, duration, and persistence are unspecified; the available instantaneous tone checks cannot reliably require a potentially brief boundary alarm, so audible alarm behavior is not independently covered.",
  "assumptions": [
    "Uses the disclosed bench defaults: D2 and D3 buttons connect to GND, use INPUT_PULLUP, and are pressed LOW. Authoritative pins are CLK D4, DIO D5, and buzzer D6.",
    "No initial count is specified. Twenty separate decrement presses establish zero from any legal initial value in 0..20; no particular startup value is required.",
    "A separate press increments or decrements once. Each test press lasts 200 ms and is followed by at least 300 ms released time, allowing ordinary debounce implementations to settle.",
    "Alarm frequency, duration, and whether it persists at a boundary are missing. The reference chooses a brief 1000 Hz alarm and starts at zero; these choices are not imposed by the checks.",
    "Display comparisons are numeric, permitting leading blanks or zeros."
  ],
